## Reading
- M1 (no release flush): only the AC-005 termination case fails -> the termination case proves the releasePreparation flush.
- M2 (no handleClientClosed flush): all pass, expected. On app-server exit the router calls
  thread.handleClientClosed (flush) and then the manager's handleUnexpectedThreadClosure ->
  releasePreparation (flush). Either one writes the pending summary; the thread-level flush is the
  synchronous one and does not depend on releaseRuntimeInput() succeeding. After this check the client-close
  case was strengthened to wait until the manager released the closed thread and then assert the
  summary was written exactly once (no double count across both flush paths).
- M3 (unbounded logging): all 4 cases fail -> every case proves the bound.
